@startuml
title Doctor project-creation application workflow

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam ParticipantPadding 12
skinparam BoxPadding 8

actor "Authenticated active\ndoctor applicant" as Doctor
participant "Flutter\n(project application)" as Flutter
participant "Management API\n/project-requests" as API
database "Immutable request ledger\nprofessional_project_requests" as Ledger
actor "Platform administrator" as Admin
actor "Target institution\nlegal representative" as LegalRep
database "Projects\nprojects" as Projects
database "Institution projects\ninstitution_projects" as InstitutionProjects
database "Applicant bindings\ndoctor_projects" as DoctorProjects
database "Applicant split configs\ndoctor_institution_project_configs" as Configs

note over Doctor,Ledger
  No doctor selector exists. The authenticated doctor is stored as the
  sole applicant and is the only doctor binding created after approval.
  Submitted request fields are immutable snapshots.
end note

group Platform-project application
  Doctor -> Flutter: enter complete platform project form
  Flutter -> API: POST /platform\nall exact 13 keys; every key present
  API -> API: require active DOCTOR\nvalidate text, arrays, money, count
  API -> Ledger: INSERT PLATFORM snapshot (PENDING, applicant doctor)
  Ledger --> API: request id
  API --> Flutter: {id, requestType: PLATFORM, status: PENDING}

  Admin -> API: POST /api/admin/project-requests/{id}/review\n{decision: APPROVED|REJECTED, reviewNote}
  API -> Ledger: lock pending immutable snapshot
  API -> API: require platform administrator\nREJECTED requires non-blank note
  alt APPROVED
    group one transaction
      API -> Projects: INSERT project\nrating = 0, review_count = 0
      API -> Ledger: close APPROVED + resultingProjectId
    end
  else REJECTED
    API -> Ledger: close REJECTED + review note
  end
  API --> Admin: review result
end

group Institution-project application
  Doctor -> Flutter: choose approved institution + platform project
  Flutter -> API: GET /institution-form-config
  API --> Flutter: {platformRate} (read only)
  Flutter -> API: POST /institutions/{institutionId}\nall exact 18 keys; null/blank/[] inherits
  API -> API: require applicant approved relationship\nvalidate inheritance, money, count and split
  API -> Ledger: INSERT INSTITUTION snapshot (PENDING, applicant doctor)
  Ledger --> API: request id
  API --> Flutter: {id, requestType: INSTITUTION, status: PENDING}

  alt Target institution legal representative
    LegalRep -> API: POST /api/management/project-requests/{id}/review
    API -> API: require current managedInstitutionIds authority
  else Platform administrator
    Admin -> API: POST /api/management/project-requests/{id}/review
    API -> API: require administrator authority
  end
  API -> Ledger: lock pending immutable snapshot
  API -> API: revalidate current institution, applicant relationship,\nplatform project, uniqueness, current platform rate and split
  alt REJECTED
    API -> Ledger: close REJECTED + non-blank review note
  else APPROVED
    group one atomic transaction; rollback all writes on any failure
      API -> InstitutionProjects: INSERT effective inherited content\nrating = 0, review_count = 0
      API -> DoctorProjects: INSERT binding for applicant doctor only
      API -> Configs: INSERT applicant split configuration
      API -> Ledger: close APPROVED + resultingInstitutionProjectId
    end
  end
  alt any write or revalidation fails
    API -> API: rollback transaction; ledger remains PENDING
    API --> Flutter: 409/error; no partial project, binding, or config
  else transaction succeeds
    API --> Flutter: review result
  end
end

note over InstitutionProjects,Configs
  Approval order is fixed: institution_projects -> doctor_projects(applicant)
  -> doctor_institution_project_configs -> close request. Reviewers never
  edit submitted fields. JOIN and PROFILE_UPDATE use separate contracts.
end note

@enduml
